<title>USA: Tambrands to take Q3 charge to consolidate.</title>
<headline>Tambrands to take Q3 charge to consolidate.</headline>
<dateline>WHITE PLAINS, N.Y. 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tambrands Inc said Wednesday it would take a $46 million pretax third quarter charge to close four of its nine manufacturing facilities, cut 17 percent of its workforce, and consolidate its domestic and international groups.  </p>
<p>The third quarter charge amounts to $1 a share, after taxes, the company said.</p>
<p>The restructuring will result in pre-tax annual savings of about $20 million, which will be recognized by the beginning of 1998, Tambrands said.</p>
<p>Edward Fogarty, Tambrands president and chief executive, will also assume the position of chairman. He succeeds Howard Wentz Jr, who will remain a director, the company said.</p>
<p>Thomas Mason, a Tambrands group vice president, was promoted to executive vice president and chief operating officer, a newly created position.</p>
<p>Mason will assume day-to-day responsibility for Tambrands' worldwide operations.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
